<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lydians</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lydians were the people of the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lydia">Lydia</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. They were known for their cavalry and wealth, and for being among the first to mint coins. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrus-the-great">Cyrus the Great</a>'s conquest of Lydia, Lydians became subjects of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a>, which drew on its subject peoples for military service.</p></div>
